{"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What is kept."}]},{"text":" Only events of the types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other, are never written, and produce no drop report, but are lost if the app ends first.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as its span ended with the earlier run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A segment kept for one undelivered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record keeps its delivered ones too. Only recovery rewrites a segment: one still holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records after it drops some (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bound.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The log never holds more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered yields a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A record too large for an empty log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is kept in memory only."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Recovery.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Other versions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional one added since is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored at another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persisten